toggle-word-wrap.ts is adapted from Microsoft Visual Studio Code (MIT):
  vendor/vscode commit d3d31f62268b169a2dfab62ffb2d7d38158a5b7c
  src/vs/workbench/contrib/codeEditor/browser/toggleWordWrap.ts
  https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/d3d31f62268b169a2dfab62ffb2d7d38158a5b7c/src/vs/workbench/contrib/codeEditor/browser/toggleWordWrap.ts

Preserved: command ID, Alt+Z binding, actual wrappingColumn decision, transient
model property and lifetime, override/reset-to-inherit semantics, configuration
and model listeners, reentrancy guard, diff-side synchronization and inline guard.
transient-model-properties.ts copies the transient-property methods and model
disposal watcher from the same revision's
  src/vs/editor/browser/services/abstractCodeEditorService.ts
These methods are stripped from standalone Monaco; the port preserves their
URI-keyed storage, change events, equality checks and model-disposal lifetime.

Adaptations: the original EditorAction registration is retained. Standalone
creation hooks replace workbench controller registration and dependency injection.
Controllers apply the initial model at
creation and dispose subscriptions with their editor. Workbench menus/context-key
tracking are omitted; Setdown's existing Wrap display command calls this action.
The inline-diff guard reads _options.renderSideBySide.get(), the exact expression
in the upstream getter that is also stripped from standalone Monaco.
No persistent preference is written by Alt+Z. Different files are independent;
views sharing a model share the toggle, just as in VS Code.

